---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = 'July 2026';
---

<Base title="Terms & Usage Policy · HyphaeHub" description="The terms and acceptable-use policy for HyphaeHub.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-substrate">Terms &amp; Usage Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/50">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <p>
          These terms are an agreement between you and HyphaeHub LLC ("HyphaeHub", "we", "us") for
          use of the HyphaeHub website, hosted Cloud service, and mobile app (together, the
          "Service"). By using the Service, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do
          not use it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">The Service and its editions</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          HyphaeHub is a record-keeping tool for mushroom cultivation. It comes in three forms: a
          free, open-source Community Edition you host yourself; a hosted Cloud service with free and
          paid plans; and a mobile app. Some features are offered behind flags and may change or be
          removed as we develop them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Your account</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You are responsible for the accuracy of your account details, for keeping your sign-in
          secure, and for activity in your organization, including members you invite and the roles
          you assign them. Tell us promptly if you suspect unauthorized access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">HyphaeHub is species-agnostic and is provided for record-keeping only. When you use it, you agree that you will:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Use the Service only for lawful purposes, and comply with every law and regulation that applies to what you cultivate and how you cultivate it in your jurisdiction.</li>
          <li>Not use the Service to plan, promote, or facilitate any illegal activity.</li>
          <li>Only enter data you have the right to enter, and respect the privacy of anyone in your organization.</li>
          <li>Not attempt to breach security, access other users' data without authorization, scrape or overload the Service, or interfere with its operation.</li>
          <li>Not upload malware or unlawful, infringing, or harmful content.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may suspend or remove access that violates this policy. Nothing here restricts the
          rights granted to you for the Community Edition under its open-source license.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Plans, billing, and cancellation</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Paid plans are billed through Stripe on a recurring basis until cancelled. You can change
          or cancel your plan at any time from the billing settings, and cancellation takes effect at
          the end of the current billing period. Fees are exclusive of taxes where they apply. We may
          change prices or plan limits with reasonable advance notice. Except where the law requires
          otherwise, payments are non-refundable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Your content and our intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Your records are yours. You grant us the limited license needed to store and process them
          so we can provide the Service to you. We own the HyphaeHub name, brand, and the hosted
          Service itself. The Community Edition source is provided under the MIT license, and those
          license terms govern your use of that code.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Disclaimers</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The Service is a record-keeping tool. It is not agricultural, legal, financial, or medical
          advice, and it does not guarantee any cultivation outcome. The Service is provided "as is"
          and "as available", without warranties of any kind, to the fullest extent allowed by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, HyphaeHub will not be liable for indirect,
          incidental, or consequential damages, or for lost profits, data, or crops. Our total
          liability for any claim relating to the Service will not exceed the greater of the amount
          you paid us in the twelve months before the claim, or one hundred US dollars.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Indemnification</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You agree to indemnify and hold HyphaeHub harmless from claims arising out of your use of
          the Service or your violation of these terms or applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Termination</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You may stop using the Service at any time. We may suspend or end access if you violate
          these terms. You can export your data before you leave, and our Privacy Policy explains how
          deletion works.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Governing law and venue</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Oregon, without regard to its
          conflict-of-law rules. You agree that any dispute relating to the Service will be brought
          exclusively in the state or federal courts located in Deschutes County, Oregon, with venue
          in Sisters, Oregon, and you consent to the jurisdiction of those courts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We may update these terms from time to time. When we make material changes, we will update
          the date above and, where appropriate, notify you. Continued use after a change means you
          accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-substrate">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Questions about these terms? Email
          <a class="font-medium text-hyphae-700 hover:underline" href="mailto:support@hyphaehub.io">support@hyphaehub.io</a>.
          See also our
          <a class="font-medium text-hyphae-700 hover:underline" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
